            <ArticleTitle>Cervical cord and dorsal medullary infarction presenting with retro-orbital pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>632-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 36-year-old woman experienced an excruciating right retro-orbital paroxysmal headache after a stroke of the anterior two-thirds of the right hemicord at the C1 level (anterior spinal artery territory) and the dorsal medulla (posterior spinal artery territory). A right vertebral artery dissection was demonstrated. This unusual infarct mimicked a cluster headache attack or paroxysmal hemicrania.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
